#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# boole

#% text
# `boole(b)` gives `1` for `true` and `0` for `false`; on a list it works element by element. Any other argument stays as it is.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
boole([true, false, true])
#% output
#= [1, 0, 1]

#% cell
boole(x > 0)
#% output
#= boole(x > 0)

#% cell
total(boole(map(is_prime, range(100))))
#% output
#= 25

#% section
# See also

#% text
